{
 "_about": [
  "Curated lay-language aliases per specialty: the symptoms and everyday words a",
  "caller actually uses, in English and Spanish.",
  "",
  "This is the highest-leverage data in the retrieval layer. Embedding a bare",
  "label ('Orthopedics') against a complaint ('me duele la rodilla') is a weak",
  "match, because the link is clinical inference rather than similarity. The",
  "index embeds an enriched document per specialty -- name + its appointment type",
  "names + these aliases -- which gives the complaint something real to match.",
  "",
  "They also power the lexical channel, which is what catches rare exact tokens",
  "(MRI, DEXA, mamografia) that embeddings handle badly, and which works with no",
  "network at all. In a production system this vocabulary is owned by the clinic."
 ],
